SquaredAnt GmbH grants you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable license
to install and use the extension for your own personal, academic, professional,
or business document-registration workflows.

You may not sell, sublicense, commercially redistribute, or present modified
versions of the extension as an official SquaredAnt or DigitalOwnership release
without written permission from SquaredAnt GmbH.

3. Service Terms And Privacy

Use of the DigitalOwnership web service, purchased registration credits, Stripe
payment flow, support functions, and hosted account features is governed by the
current terms and privacy information published at:

https://digitalownership.squaredant.com/terms
https://digitalownership.squaredant.com/privacy

This extension license governs installation and local use of the LibreOffice
extension. The published service terms govern website accounts, payments,
registration credits, support, and other hosted service features.

4. Document Content And Local Records

The extension is designed to calculate a document fingerprint locally. Users
should not share unpublished or non-public manuscripts with SquaredAnt GmbH or
any other party unless they deliberately choose to do so outside the extension.

The extension creates an archive copy for the user's records when registration
starts and marks that copy read-only on the user's computer. File permissions
may not survive email, cloud-sync, or cross-platform transfer. Registration
details such as document fingerprint, algorithm scope, transaction hash,
blockchain explorer link, and registration time may be stored in a hidden local
DigitalOwnership records folder beside the archive. These local records support
later verification but do not replace the blockchain registration.

Users remain responsible for keeping their own document files, backups, archive
copies, and access credentials.

5. Blockchain Transactions

Blockchain transactions are submitted to public blockchain networks. Public
blockchain data may be permanent, visible to third parties, and difficult or
impossible to remove.

Blockchain network operating costs, sometimes called gas costs, may vary. A
registration using purchased credits may be delayed or blocked when network
costs are unusually high. Direct wallet registrations are made at the user's own
risk and cost.

6. Wallets, Keys, And Account Security

You are responsible for your wallet, private keys, passwords, email account,
computer security, and document access controls. SquaredAnt GmbH cannot recover
lost private keys, lost wallets, deleted documents, or inaccessible accounts
unless a separate recovery mechanism is expressly provided.

Never store production private keys in document files, extension files, or other
locations that are not designed for secret storage.

